        "id": 6705,
        "name": "logan_mann",
        "username": "logan_mann",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/43a26b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-21T03:52:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I was hoping to get some feedback on an idea.</p><p>I love the modifier tokens, but there are often times that something affects a vast multitude of targets and suddenly tokens seem in short supply.&nbsp; I've been trying to find a useful solution.&nbsp; My best effort is a card (I made is the same dimensions as an oversized card) that represents global groups.</p><p>It has sections for</p><p>All Hero Targets</p><p>All Environment Targets</p><p>All Villain Targets</p><p>So if something affects all heroes...you place the token there.&nbsp; If it affects all Non-Environment cards you place one of the appropriate token on the all heroes and another one on all villains.</p><p>This seems to be functional...but I wonder if others have a better solution to the problem...or if they would suggest another breakdown of sections on the card.</p><p>I can't seem to get a picture to show up here but I could get it to load on BGG so heres a link to show what I'm using now.</p><p><a href=\"http://www.boardgamegeek.com/image/1481544/logan_mann\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.boardgamegeek.com/image/1481544/logan_mann</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:44.915Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
